# Line endings: normalise to LF in the repository.
#
# This project is explicit about LF: a CRLF shell script fails under bash with a
# misleading error (`pipefail: invalid option name`), and the WSL execution layer
# is where every real run happens. Without this file, Git on Windows would store
# CRLF and break those scripts for anyone who clones on Linux.
#
# `text=auto` still lets Git detect binary files and leave them alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending-translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.safetensors binary
*.bin binary
*.pt binary
*.pyc binary

# Explicit LF for files where it is functionally required.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

# Windows-only helper scripts would want CRLF, but this repo has none committed
# (execution helpers live in the gitignored .scripts/).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Generated or vendored trees: keep Git from trying to diff them as text.
*.lock -diff